WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.871
About 24 custom

00:00:01.683 --> 00:00:02.673
kernels to run

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:03.215
Inkling on a

00:00:03.027 --> 00:00:03.640
Mac

00:00:04.158 --> 00:00:05.667
Developer David Dalcu

00:00:05.479 --> 00:00:06.516
added support for

00:00:06.328 --> 00:00:07.341
Thinking Machines'

00:00:07.153 --> 00:00:08.308
Inkling 2 Mini

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:09.311
to MLX-Serve

00:00:09.559 --> 00:00:10.478
his server for

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:11.870
running models locally

00:00:11.682 --> 00:00:12.849
on Apple Silicon

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:13.367
Macs

00:00:13.894 --> 00:00:14.943
After writing about

00:00:14.755 --> 00:00:16.323
24 custom kernels

00:00:16.547 --> 00:00:17.195
he says it

00:00:17.007 --> 00:00:17.679
might be the

00:00:17.491 --> 00:00:18.622
fastest way to

00:00:18.446 --> 00:00:19.177
run the model

00:00:18.988 --> 00:00:19.601
on a Mac

00:00:19.413 --> 00:00:20.026
today

00:00:20.558 --> 00:00:21.737
The pre-release ships

00:00:21.572 --> 00:00:22.197
8-bit

00:00:22.445 --> 00:00:24.732
NVFP4 and MXFP8

00:00:24.544 --> 00:00:25.227
versions

00:00:25.346 --> 00:00:26.371
with an 8-bit

00:00:26.195 --> 00:00:27.161
build on Hugging

00:00:26.973 --> 00:00:27.633
Face

00:00:27.772 --> 00:00:29.010
A 4-bit version

00:00:28.822 --> 00:00:29.717
did not pass

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:30.519
his quality bar

00:00:30.331 --> 00:00:30.814
yet

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:32.364
Full story on

00:00:32.175 --> 00:00:33.071
the dashboard
